I rewrote the LP page (`specdojo-lp:src/pages/index.astro`) with the structure and copy from the ticket, but the Astro build has not been run. Running npm in the LP repo needs approval in this sandbox, so `npm run build` still has to be run outside it.

**Why I rewrote it:** the ticket (`pjr-hepk-lp-content.md`) already said the content had been put into `index.astro`, but the file was still the placeholder page. The earlier run's changes appear not to have been kept, so I wrote the page again following the ticket's section 4.1.

**What the page now contains:**
- **Header:** the service name and a link to the docs site.
- **Hero:** the tagline "決めて、書いて、鍛え続ける。", a button to the 5-step section, and a link to Quick Start. The mascot spot is only a dashed placeholder box marked `data-placeholder="mascot"`.
- **Three problems:** decisions are scattered, nobody can trace "why", and AI has to be given the background every time.
- **How register works:** you file issue / decision / todo items, each item's Markdown file is the source of record, and the lists are generated from those files.
- **Five steps to start:** install, then `npx specdojo config init`, `register scaffold --project prj-0001`, `register add --project prj-0001 --type issue --title "..."`, and `register build --project prj-0001`.
- **Next steps:** links to Quick Start, the register operation guide, the command reference and the overview guide.
- **Footer:** copyright and a docs-site link.
- **Styling:** only the theme classes from PJR-CM5W's `global.css`.

**Checks I did:**
- **Command options:** checked against `src/specdojo-config.ts` and `src/register.ts`. `config init` takes no arguments and creates `prj-0001` with the register at `controls/project-register`. `register add` requires `--type` and `--title`. They also match the command reference and the Quick Start guide.
- **Doc links:** all five pages (the `ja/` top page, Quick Start, register operation guide, command reference, overview guide) load on the public docs site.
- **Ticket:** I left it unchanged because its structure, description of the work and remaining issues already match the new page. Task 3 stays open because the build is unconfirmed. I did not touch the result file, the register status or Git.
- **Other checks:**
  - The LP repo has no Prettier, so formatting was skipped.
  - I changed nothing under `docs/`, so `specdojo index build` doesn't apply.
  - prj-0002 has no `catalog_path`, so `catalog validate` doesn't apply.
  - The parent runner runs its listed checks itself after this stage.

